# Ownership for eshu-workflow (Refs eshu-hq/eshu#8875, criterion C3).
#
# Accountable owner for implementation, public contract, and release:
# @linuxdynasty. Every entry below names that owner; the entries exist so
# review routing distinguishes the three responsibilities instead of
# leaving them implicit.
#
# Production target: the owner-designated QA EKS environment (ops-qa).
# Deployment configuration source: boatsgroup/iac-eks-eshu (a separate
# repo under devops ownership). Nothing in this repo deploys; a Satellite
# change here reaches ops-qa only through a reviewed pin roll there.
#
# The split below mirrors the workflow.v1 plane declaration
# (workflowv1/doc.go): the claim plane (collectors claim, heartbeat,
# complete, release, fail; core pins a claim server-side before
# committing), the report plane (core pushes run progress), and the read
# plane (run status, lists, completeness, instances, queue depth). The
# public contract names the planes; the implementation serves them; the
# release lines ship them. Contract changes move both sides at once, so
# the contract entry is separate from the implementation entries.

# Default: everything in this repo needs the accountable owner.
* @linuxdynasty

# Public contract: workflow.v1 (protocol name, major, RouteTable, planes,
# closed enums, error and version headers). Shared with the core callers;
# a closed-enum addition is a major protocol bump.
# Planes served: claim, report, read.
/workflowv1/ @linuxdynasty

# Implementation: the claim-plane server, the coordinator, and the HTTP
# client they share. No entry here changes the contract.
/cmd/ @linuxdynasty
/coordinator/ @linuxdynasty
/server/ @linuxdynasty
/store/ @linuxdynasty
/client/ @linuxdynasty
/internal/ @linuxdynasty

# Release and supply chain: what ops-qa pins and what feeds it.
# image-publish.yml publishes ghcr.io/eshu-hq/eshu-workflow on main and
# version-tag pushes; Dependabot proposes the grouped weekly bumps.
/Dockerfile @linuxdynasty
/.dockerignore @linuxdynasty
/.github/workflows/image-publish.yml @linuxdynasty
/.github/dependabot.yml @linuxdynasty
/go.mod @linuxdynasty
/go.sum @linuxdynasty
